  "repo_truth": "The original HCM-3.5 planning discovery is CLEAN but had a named product decision stop. The exact user authority and completed different-parent attestation now permit only its direct documentation-planning continuation. Existing Flow and pipeline callers are evidence for a future call-path plan, not a legacy compatibility constraint. GitNexus MCP/CLI/index remains unavailable and is recorded as unavailable, never green.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Create the continuation selector and authority-admission/continuation proof records, and update only grant-ceiling HCM-3.5 planning and membrane documentation to make the resolved plan implementation-ready.",
    "Freeze a planned typed handbook-engine/handbook-flow/handbook-pipeline owner boundary and greenfield cutover posture; plan future standalone Handbook CLI and crates.io SDK/library composition for a Substrate wrapper while Tier 2 bundled binary/JSON remains transitional.",
    "Plan only a typed non-promoting evidence boundary and a bounded, redacted engine-produced delta-signal summary reconciled with reveal_delta_signals; preserve the immutable relation-only snapshot_delta and distinguish local completion from parent promotion."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "Do not change Rust, runtime or product behavior, public APIs, schemas, configuration, dependencies, SDK/CLI/Substrate implementation, consumer adoption, publication, registry proof, or HCM-3.6.",
    "Do not edit any path outside the continuation grant ceiling, protected checkout, handoff record, ledger, or other global closeout surface.",
    "Do not fetch, query, or push remote state; merge, rebase, reset, clean, force-update, stage, commit, or update refs."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Read the complete dispatch, cited authority, current source seams as read-only context, and the live 00-09 membrane documents before writing the smallest coherent documentation plan.",
    "Write exact planned ownership, call-path, fail-closed and proof seams without selecting a Rust signature, public API, schema, package publication, or consumer change.",
    "Return changed files, implementation-ready decisions, validation evidence, GitNexus availability result, and every blocker or uncertainty to the parent; do not create global handoff or ledger state."
  ],
  "contracts_and_gates": [
    "This is the sole non-review documentation write in the implementation stage after the independent authority-admission CLEAN result. The following review must be fresh, complete-subject, and independent.",
    "The plan must keep local completion non-promoting, treat unresolved/omitted/redacted/stale evidence as fail-closed, and never route generic snapshot_delta reads into Flow or pipeline.",
    "No real runtime, package, registry, or adoption claim is established by documentation planning."
  ],
  "stop_conditions": [
    "Return BLOCKED without expanding scope if the requested documentation plan requires product behavior, a public surface, a schema/configuration change, protected path, remote operation, or new authority.",
    "Return BLOCKED if a required source/authority contradiction cannot be resolved solely in the grant's documentation ceiling.",
    "Report all results to the parent through the built-in channel without creating durable global closeout state."
  ],
